IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cdcsa-types`
IMPORT `cdcsa-common`

-- Child Development Co-Savings Act 2001 — GOALS 3 AND 4: MOTHERS
-- (maternity: ss 9, 9A, 10, 12; adoption: ss 12A, 12AA-12AD).
--
--   "Is she eligible; how many weeks of paid leave; how much must the
--    employer pay, and how much of it may the employer claim back; what may
--    a self-employed mother claim; and, if she has neither, what Government-
--    paid benefit?"
--
-- Amounts are computed from the parent's gross pay (or lost income) per week
-- of work days. A "block" is a period of 4 times the weekly index or 24 days,
-- whichever is lower, which is 4 weeks of work days.
-- Source: ../source/CDCSA2001.txt lines 568-1922.

§ `Goals 3-4 — mothers`

DECLARE `Leave payments` HAS
    `weeks of paid leave`                IS A NUMBER
    `employer pays at most`              IS A NUMBER
    `Government reimburses the employer at most` IS A NUMBER

§§ `Eligibility for maternity leave and benefits (s 9A)`

-- s 9A(1): "(a) her confinement ... occurs, or the estimated delivery date ...
-- is, on or after 1 January 2017, or (in the case of a stillborn child) on or
-- after 1 November 2021; (b) a child delivered ... is a citizen of Singapore at
-- the time of the child's birth, or (in the case of a stillborn child) would
-- have been ...; (c) in the case of a female employee, she has served her
-- employer for a period of at least 3 months before the day of her
-- confinement; and (d) in the case of a self-employed woman, she has been
-- carrying on her trade ... for a continuous period of at least 3 months".
@ref s 9A(1)
GIVEN months IS A NUMBER, b IS A Birth
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `eligible under s 9A(1), with months of service` months `, for` b IF
        `the confinement date gate` b
    AND b's `a citizen at birth (or would have been, if stillborn)`
    AND months AT LEAST 3

GIVEN b IS A Birth
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the confinement date gate` b IF
        b's `confinement on` AT LEAST `gate`
    OR  b's `estimated delivery date` AT LEAST `gate`
    WHERE
        `gate` MEANS IF b's `stillborn` THEN YMD 2021 11 1 ELSE YMD 2017 1 1

-- s 9A(1A): (a) on or after 1 January 2017; "(b) a child delivered ... (i) is
-- not a citizen of Singapore at the time of the child's birth; but (ii)
-- becomes a citizen of Singapore within the period of 12 months commencing on
-- the date of the child's birth"; (c)-(d) 3 months.
@ref s 9A(1A)
GIVEN months IS A NUMBER, b IS A Birth
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `eligible under s 9A(1A), with months of service` months `, for` b IF
        (b's `confinement on` AT LEAST YMD 2017 1 1 OR b's `estimated delivery date` AT LEAST YMD 2017 1 1)
    AND NOT b's `a citizen at birth (or would have been, if stillborn)`
    AND `becomes a citizen within 12 months of birth` b
    AND months AT LEAST 3

GIVEN b IS A Birth
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `becomes a citizen within 12 months of birth` b IF
    CONSIDER b's `became a citizen on`
    WHEN JUST d  THEN d LESS THAN `add years` (b's `confinement on`) 1
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

-- s 9A(2): Government-paid maternity benefit: (a) the date gate as (1)(a);
-- (b) a citizen at birth or within 12 months; "(c) for at least 90 days in the
-- aggregate during the period of 12 months immediately before the day of her
-- confinement, she has been employed by one or more employers, self-employed
-- or both (whether in Singapore or outside Singapore)"; (d) the overseas
-- conditions. Days are counted under s 9A(2A) by the caller.
@ref s 9A(2), (2A)
GIVEN b IS A Birth, w IS A `Work facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `eligible for the Government-paid maternity benefit under s 9A(2)` b w IF
        `the confinement date gate` b
    AND (b's `a citizen at birth (or would have been, if stillborn)` OR `becomes a citizen within 12 months of birth` b)
    AND w's `days employed or self-employed in the 12 months before` AT LEAST 90
    AND w's `the 90-day overseas conditions are met, if any days were outside Singapore`

§§ `Maternity leave and its payment (ss 9(1), 9A(4), 10)`

-- s 9(1): "absent herself from work — (a) during — (i) the period of 4 weeks
-- immediately before her confinement; and (ii) the period of 12 weeks
-- immediately after ...; (b) during a period of 16 weeks, as agreed ...; or
-- (c) during — (i) a period of 8 weeks ...; and (ii) one or more than one later
-- period ... in aggregate ... equal in duration to 8 times the employee's
-- weekly index or 48 days (whichever is the lower) ... within the period of 12
-- months commencing on the day of her confinement" — each at "her gross rate
-- of pay". Sixteen weeks in every arrangement.
-- s 9A(4): the payment "is subject to the following amounts": (a) first or
-- second specified event: "$10,000 for every period ... equal in duration to 4
-- times the employee's weekly index or every 24 days, whichever is the lower,
-- of her absence ... after the first 8 weeks", "in any case ... a total of
-- $20,000"; (b) third or subsequent: $10,000 for every such period of her
-- absence, "a total of $40,000".
-- s 10(1)-(2): the employer may claim back (a) for a first or second event,
-- the amount paid "for the period of her absence ... after the first 8 weeks";
-- (b) for a third or later, "the whole period", with the CPF contributions on
-- it, up to $10,000 a period and $20,000 or $40,000 in all.
-- s 12E(7): a mother who elects N weeks to the father has her entitlement
-- "reduced by N weeks, taken from the last N weeks of that entitlement", so
-- the weeks given up come off the capped weeks first.
@ref ss 9(1), 9A(4), 10(1)-(2), 12E(7)
GIVEN event IS A NUMBER, `weeks given up` IS A NUMBER, `gross per week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Leave payments`
`maternity leave payments, specified event` event `, weeks given up under s 12E` `weeks given up` `, gross pay per week` `gross per week` MEANS
    `leave payments of` 16 (IF `a first or second specified event` event THEN 8 ELSE 0) (IF `a first or second specified event` event THEN 20000 ELSE 40000) `weeks given up` `gross per week`

-- The shape the maternity and adoption caps share: of `weeks` of leave, the
-- first `uncapped weeks` are paid at gross and not reimbursed; the rest are
-- paid at gross up to $10,000 a 4-week block and `total` in all, and that part
-- is reimbursed. Weeks given up under s 12E(7) come off the end.
GIVEN weeks IS A NUMBER, `uncapped weeks` IS A NUMBER, total IS A NUMBER, `given up` IS A NUMBER, `gross per week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Leave payments`
`leave payments of` weeks `uncapped weeks` total `given up` `gross per week` MEANS
    `Leave payments` WITH
        `weeks of paid leave`                        IS `remaining`
        `employer pays at most`                      IS `uncapped part` TIMES `gross per week` PLUS `capped`
        `Government reimburses the employer at most` IS `capped`
    WHERE
        `remaining`     MEANS IF weeks MINUS `given up` LESS THAN 0 THEN 0 ELSE weeks MINUS `given up`
        `uncapped part` MEANS IF `remaining` LESS THAN `uncapped weeks` THEN `remaining` ELSE `uncapped weeks`
        `capped weeks`  MEANS `remaining` MINUS `uncapped part`
        `capped`        MEANS `at most` 10000 `per block and` total `in all, for` (`capped weeks` DIVIDED BY 4) `blocks paid at` (4 TIMES `gross per week`)

-- s 9(1)(c)(ii): the later periods total "8 times the employee's weekly index
-- or 48 days (whichever is the lower)".
@ref s 9(1)(c)(ii); First Schedule note 5
GIVEN wi IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the flexible maternity days for weekly index` wi MEANS `the lower of` 8 `times the weekly index` wi `or` 48

-- s 9(4)-(5), 9A(5): a self-employed mother claims lost income from the
-- Government: (5)(a) first or second event, "for the period of her cessation
-- ... which is after the first 8 weeks"; (b) third or later, "the whole
-- period"; capped as for an employee ($10,000 a period; $20,000 or $40,000).
@ref ss 9(4)-(5), 9A(5)
GIVEN event IS A NUMBER, `lost income per week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Government pays a self-employed mother at most, specified event` event `, lost income per week` `lost income per week` MEANS
    IF `a first or second specified event` event
    THEN `at most` 10000 `per block and` 20000 `in all, for` 2 `blocks paid at` (4 TIMES `lost income per week`)
    ELSE `at most` 10000 `per block and` 40000 `in all, for` 4 `blocks paid at` (4 TIMES `lost income per week`)

-- s 9(2): a female employee who "has worked in her employment for any day
-- during the benefit period before her confinement" is entitled "(a) to
-- receive, in addition to her gross rate of pay for that day, an amount that
-- is equivalent to a day's pay ...; or (b) to absent herself from work on
-- another day at the end of the benefit period".
@ref s 9(2)
GIVEN `days worked` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`extra days' pay (or days off at the end) for days worked before confinement in the benefit period` `days worked` MEANS `days worked`

§§ `A child who becomes a citizen later (s 9(1A), (1B))`

-- s 9(1A): where the mother is absent under s 76(1) of the Employment Act 1968
-- (which is not in the source: its "specified period" is an input), what this
-- Act adds turns on the limb of s 76(1), the event number, and when the child
-- becomes a citizen.
DECLARE `EA s 76(1) limb` IS ONE OF
    `(a)`
    `(b)`
    `(c)`

DECLARE `s 9(1A) outcome` IS ONE OF
    `pay for the last 4 weeks of the specified period, and a further 4 weeks or the agreed flexible period`
    `pay from citizenship to the end of the specified period, and a further 4 weeks or the agreed flexible period`
    `a further 4 weeks or the agreed flexible period, from citizenship`
    `pay for every s 76(1)(c)(ii) period, and later periods totalling 4 times the weekly index or 24 days`
    `pay from citizenship to the end of the eight-week period and for every s 76(1)(c)(ii) period, and later periods totalling 4 times the weekly index or 24 days`
    `pay for every s 76(1)(c)(ii) period from citizenship, and later periods from citizenship totalling 4 times the weekly index or 24 days`
    `nothing under s 9(1A)`

-- (i), (iii): first or second event, limb (a) or (b). "(A) if the child
-- becomes a citizen ... within the first 4 weeks [(b): 8 weeks] of the
-- [specified period] — ... the last 4 weeks of the specified period; and ... a
-- further period of 4 weeks ...; (B) ... after the first 4 [8] weeks of, but
-- within, the specified period — ... the day the child becomes a citizen ...
-- [to] the last day of the specified period; and ... a further period of 4
-- weeks ...; or (C) ... within a period of 4 weeks commencing immediately
-- after the specified period ends, ... a further period of 4 weeks commencing
-- on the day the child becomes a citizen".
-- (ii), (iv): third or later event: (A) within the specified period — pay
-- from citizenship to its end, and a further 4 weeks; (B) within the 4 weeks
-- after — a further 4 weeks from citizenship.
-- (iva): limb (a) or (b), citizenship "after the period of 16 weeks, which
-- commences on the first day on which she exercised her entitlement under
-- section 76(1)(a) or (b) ..., but within the period of 12 months commencing
-- on the day of her confinement" — a further 4 weeks from citizenship.
-- (v)-(vi): limb (c), against "the period of 8 weeks referred to in
-- section 76(1)(c)(i)".
@ref s 9(1A)(i)-(vi), (1AA)
GIVEN limb IS AN `EA s 76(1) limb`, event IS A NUMBER, `period starts` IS A DATE, `period ends` IS A DATE, `first day of absence` IS A DATE, confinement IS A DATE, citizen IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `s 9(1A) outcome`
`the s 9(1A) outcome under s 76(1)` limb `, specified event` event `, the specified period from` `period starts` `to` `period ends` `, absence from` `first day of absence` `, confinement` confinement `, citizen on` citizen MEANS
    CONSIDER limb
    WHEN `(c)` THEN
        BRANCH IF citizen AT MOST `period ends` AND `a first or second specified event` event
                  THEN `pay for every s 76(1)(c)(ii) period, and later periods totalling 4 times the weekly index or 24 days`
               IF citizen AT MOST `period ends`
                  THEN `pay from citizenship to the end of the eight-week period and for every s 76(1)(c)(ii) period, and later periods totalling 4 times the weekly index or 24 days`
               IF `within 12 months`
                  THEN `pay for every s 76(1)(c)(ii) period from citizenship, and later periods from citizenship totalling 4 times the weekly index or 24 days`
               OTHERWISE `nothing under s 9(1A)`
    OTHERWISE
        BRANCH IF `a first or second specified event` event AND citizen LESS THAN `period starts` PLUS `first weeks` TIMES 7
                  THEN `pay for the last 4 weeks of the specified period, and a further 4 weeks or the agreed flexible period`
               IF citizen AT MOST `period ends`
                  THEN `pay from citizenship to the end of the specified period, and a further 4 weeks or the agreed flexible period`
               IF citizen LESS THAN `period ends` PLUS 1 PLUS 28
                  THEN `a further 4 weeks or the agreed flexible period, from citizenship`
               IF citizen AT LEAST `first day of absence` PLUS 112 AND `within 12 months`
                  THEN `a further 4 weeks or the agreed flexible period, from citizenship`
               OTHERWISE `nothing under s 9(1A)`
    WHERE
        `first weeks` MEANS IF limb EQUALS `(a)` THEN 4 ELSE 8
        `within 12 months` MEANS citizen LESS THAN `add years` confinement 1

-- s 9(1B): a mother not entitled under s 76(1) of the Employment Act: "(i)
-- the period commencing on the day the child becomes a citizen ... and ending
-- on the last day of the period of 16 weeks commencing on the day of her
-- confinement; (ii) if the child becomes a citizen ... within the period of
-- 8 weeks ... — (A) [citizenship to the end of the 8 weeks] and (B) ... later
-- periods ... 8 times the employee's weekly index or 48 days ...; or (iii) if
-- ... after the period of 8 weeks ..., ... periods ... in aggregate equal ...
-- to 8 times the employee's weekly index or 48 days ..., ... on or after the
-- day the child becomes a citizen".
@ref s 9(1B)
GIVEN confinement IS A DATE, citizen IS A DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`the s 9(1B) options, confinement` confinement `, citizen on` citizen MEANS
    IF citizen LESS THAN confinement PLUS 56
    THEN LIST "(i) from citizenship to the end of the 16 weeks from confinement"
              "(ii) from citizenship to the end of the 8 weeks from confinement, and later periods totalling 8 times the weekly index or 48 days within 12 months"
    ELSE LIST "(i) from citizenship to the end of the 16 weeks from confinement"
              "(iii) periods from citizenship totalling 8 times the weekly index or 48 days within 12 months"

§§ `Forfeiture on leaving (s 9(2A), (3), (3A))`

DECLARE `Termination` IS ONE OF
    `by resignation`
    `by dismissal, completion of contract or another reason`

-- s 9(2A): if she resigns before exercising her entitlement, she forfeits the
-- unexercised leave and its pay. s 9(3)-(3A): on any other termination she
-- forfeits only the flexible later periods (s 9(1)(c)(ii), (1A)(v)-(vi),
-- (1B)(ii)(B), (iii), the agreed flexible period) and pay for the s 76(1)(c)(ii)
-- periods.
@ref s 9(2A), (3), (3A)
GIVEN t IS A `Termination`
GIVETH A STRING
`what is forfeited on termination` t MEANS
    CONSIDER t
    WHEN `by resignation` THEN "the whole unexercised entitlement to leave under s 9(1), (1A) or (1B), and its pay"
    WHEN `by dismissal, completion of contract or another reason` THEN "only the unexercised flexible later periods (s 9(1)(c)(ii), (1A)(v)-(vi), (1B)(ii)(B), (iii), the agreed flexible period) and their pay"

§§ `The Government-paid maternity benefit (s 9(5A)-(8), 9A(5A))`

-- s 9(5A): "(a) an amount equivalent to 56 days of her total income during
-- such period before delivery as may be prescribed, where her confinement ...
-- is her first or second specified event; or (b) ... 112 days ..., where ...
-- third or subsequent". s 9A(5A)(a): "an amount that does not exceed $10,000
-- for every 28 days". The prescribed period is for regulations; the caller
-- gives total income per day in it (s 9(7)-(8)).
@ref s 9(5A), 9A(5A)(a)
GIVEN event IS A NUMBER, `income per day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Government-paid maternity benefit at most, specified event` event `, total income per day` `income per day` MEANS
    `at most` 10000 `per block and` (`blocks` TIMES 10000) `in all, for` `blocks` `blocks paid at` (28 TIMES `income per day`)
    WHERE
        `blocks` MEANS IF `a first or second specified event` event THEN 2 ELSE 4

-- s 9(6): she may not claim under (5A) if she is also entitled to leave or pay
-- under s 9(1), (1A), (1B), (4) or (4A), or s 76 of the Employment Act, for the
-- same confinement, forfeited or not — "except as provided in subsections (6A)
-- and (6B)": (6A) leave without pay for a continuous period ending at least 12
-- months after delivery; (6B) she would have been entitled but for her
-- employment ending on completion of contract, redundancy or reorganisation.
@ref s 9(6), (6A), (6B)
GIVEN `entitled to leave or lost income` IS A BOOLEAN, `unpaid leave of 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN, `lost it by contract end or redundancy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `disqualified from the Government-paid maternity benefit, entitled:` `entitled to leave or lost income` `, on 12 months' unpaid leave:` `unpaid leave of 12 months` `, contract ended or redundant:` `lost it by contract end or redundancy` IF
        `entitled to leave or lost income`
    AND NOT `unpaid leave of 12 months`
    AND NOT `lost it by contract end or redundancy`

§§ `Discretionary reimbursement and directions (s 10(2A)-(3))`

-- s 10(2A)-(2B): the Government "may reimburse" an employer who pays a female
-- employee who lacks 3 months' service (s 10(2B)(e)) where "(a) the ...
-- confinement occurs, or the estimated delivery date ... is, on or after
-- 1 November 2021; (b) the child ... is a citizen ... at birth, or ... becomes
-- a citizen ... within the period of 12 months ...; (c)-(d) [the absence falls
-- within the window]".
@ref s 10(2A)-(2C)
GIVEN months IS A NUMBER, b IS A Birth, `absence within the window` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Government may reimburse under s 10(2A), months of service` months `, birth` b `, absence in window:` `absence within the window` IF
        (b's `confinement on` AT LEAST YMD 2021 11 1 OR b's `estimated delivery date` AT LEAST YMD 2021 11 1)
    AND (b's `a citizen at birth (or would have been, if stillborn)` OR `becomes a citizen within 12 months of birth` b)
    AND `absence within the window`
    AND months LESS THAN 3

-- s 10(3): no reimbursement for an amount the employer "is directed, on or
-- after 1 January 2017," to pay by the Minister for manpower, the
-- Commissioner for Labour or a court, "unless the direction has been
-- withdrawn or reversed".
@ref s 10(3)
GIVEN `directed on` IS A MAYBE DATE, `withdrawn or reversed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a directed amount is barred from reimbursement, directed on` `directed on` `, withdrawn:` `withdrawn or reversed` IF
    CONSIDER `directed on`
    WHEN JUST d  THEN d AT LEAST YMD 2017 1 1 AND NOT `withdrawn or reversed`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

§§ `Adoption (ss 12A, 12AA-12AD)`

-- s 12AC(1): "(a) the eligibility date ... is on or after 1 January 2017;
-- (b) ... served her employer for ... at least 3 months preceding the
-- eligibility date ...; (c) [self-employed: 3 months continuous]; (d) the
-- child is below 12 months of age on the eligibility date ...; (da) [a
-- permanent-resident child: she, or her joint-applicant husband, a citizen on
-- the application date]; (e) [a foreign child with a dependant's pass: a
-- citizen on the date the pass is issued]; and (f) [she] is not the natural
-- mother of the child".
@ref s 12AC(1)
GIVEN months IS A NUMBER, a IS AN Adoption
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `eligible for adoption leave under s 12AC(1), months of service` months `, adoption` a IF
        `the eligibility date of` a AT LEAST YMD 2017 1 1
    AND months AT LEAST 3
    AND `the adoption conditions` a

-- s 12AC(1)(d)-(f) and (2)(d)-(f), which s 12I(2) repeats for fathers.
@ref s 12AC(1)(d)-(f), (2)(d)-(f)
GIVEN a IS AN Adoption
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the adoption conditions` a IF
        `below 12 months of age, born` (a's `child born on`) `, on` (`the eligibility date of` a)
    AND (   NOT `a citizenship condition applies` a
         OR a's `an applicant (or the joint applicant spouse) is a citizen on the relevant date`)
    AND NOT a's `the applicant is the natural parent`

-- (da) applies to a permanent-resident child; (e) to a child neither citizen
-- nor permanent resident. A citizen child needs neither.
GIVEN a IS AN Adoption
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a citizenship condition applies` a IF
        a's `the child is a permanent resident (not a citizen) then`
    OR  NOT a's `the child is a citizen or permanent resident when the application is made`

-- s 12AC(2): the Government-paid adoption benefit: "(a) the eligibility date
-- ... on or after 1 January 2021; (b) for at least 90 days in total during the
-- period of 12 months immediately before the eligibility date ..." employed or
-- self-employed; (c) the overseas conditions; (d)-(f) as s 12AC(1).
@ref s 12AC(2)-(3)
GIVEN a IS AN Adoption, w IS A `Work facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `eligible for the Government-paid adoption benefit under s 12AC(2)` a w IF
        `the eligibility date of` a AT LEAST YMD 2021 1 1
    AND w's `days employed or self-employed in the 12 months before` AT LEAST 90
    AND w's `the 90-day overseas conditions are met, if any days were outside Singapore`
    AND `the adoption conditions` a

-- s 12AA(1): 12 weeks of adoption leave, within 12 months of the child's
-- birth: "(a) ... 12 weeks commencing on the eligibility date ...; (b) ... 12
-- weeks, as agreed ...; or (c) ... 8 weeks ... and ... later periods ... equal
-- ... to 4 times the employee's weekly index or 24 days".
-- s 12AA(4)-(5): gross rate of pay for every day, up to (a) first or second
-- event: "$10,000 for every period ... of the adoption leave ... after the
-- first 4 weeks" and "a total of $20,000"; (b) third or later: $10,000 a period
-- of all the leave, "a total of $30,000".
-- s 12AD(1)-(2): the employer claims back (a) the pay "for the period after the
-- first 4 weeks", (b) for a third or later event "the whole period", within the
-- same limits.
@ref ss 12AA(1), (4)-(6); 12AD(1)-(2); 12E(7)
GIVEN event IS A NUMBER, `weeks given up` IS A NUMBER, `gross per week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Leave payments`
`adoption leave payments, specified event` event `, weeks given up under s 12E` `weeks given up` `, gross pay per week` `gross per week` MEANS
    `leave payments of` 12 (IF `a first or second specified event` event THEN 4 ELSE 0) (IF `a first or second specified event` event THEN 20000 ELSE 30000) `weeks given up` `gross per week`

-- s 12AB(2): a self-employed woman: first or second event, $10,000 a period
-- "after the first 4 weeks of that cessation", $20,000 in all; third or later,
-- the whole cessation, $30,000.
@ref s 12AB(1)-(2)
GIVEN event IS A NUMBER, `lost income per week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Government pays a self-employed adoptive mother at most, specified event` event `, lost income per week` `lost income per week` MEANS
    IF `a first or second specified event` event
    THEN `at most` 10000 `per block and` 20000 `in all, for` 2 `blocks paid at` (4 TIMES `lost income per week`)
    ELSE `at most` 10000 `per block and` 30000 `in all, for` 3 `blocks paid at` (4 TIMES `lost income per week`)

-- s 12A(2)-(3): "(a) ... first or second specified event — an amount
-- equivalent to 56 days of her total income ...; or (b) ... third or
-- subsequent ... 84 days", "an amount that does not exceed $10,000 for every
-- 28 days".
@ref s 12A(2)-(3)
GIVEN event IS A NUMBER, `income per day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Government-paid adoption benefit at most, specified event` event `, total income per day` `income per day` MEANS
    `at most` 10000 `per block and` (`blocks` TIMES 10000) `in all, for` `blocks` `blocks paid at` (28 TIMES `income per day`)
    WHERE
        `blocks` MEANS IF `a first or second specified event` event THEN 2 ELSE 3

-- s 12AA(2): unused adoption leave lapses, without pay in lieu, if her
-- employment ends or she does not take it within 12 months of the child's
-- birth.
@ref s 12AA(2)
GIVEN `leave taken on` IS A DATE, `child born on` IS A DATE, `still employed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `adoption leave on` `leave taken on` `may still be taken, child born` `child born on` `, still employed:` `still employed` IF
        `still employed`
    AND `leave taken on` LESS THAN `add years` `child born on` 1

§§ `Provisions carried as text`

-- s 12: ss 77-82, 84, 84A and 86 of the Employment Act 1968 apply to s 9 (with
-- s 80's notice modified by s 12(1A) from 1 April 2025); Parts 13 and 16 and
-- ss 124-126 of that Act apply to disputes and offences under ss 9, 12AA, 12B,
-- 12D, 12DA, 12E, 12H and 17 (s 12(2)); ss 115-123 to claims before 1 April
-- 2017 (s 12(3)). s 12AA(1A): notice before adoption leave for an April 2025
-- Scheme child. s 12A(4)-(10), 12AD(3)-(4): reductions by regulation and
-- discretionary reimbursement, as for maternity.
@ref ss 12, 12AA(1A), 12A(4)-(10), 12AD(3)-(4)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`mothers' provisions carried as text` MEANS
    LIST "s 12(1)-(1A): Employment Act 1968 ss 77-82, 84, 84A and 86 apply to s 9 leave; s 80's notice is modified for confinements from 1 April 2025 (no notice for agreed-duration periods; otherwise the prescribed period)"
         "s 12(2)-(3): Employment Act 1968 Parts 13 and 16 and ss 124-126 (and ss 115-123 for claims lodged before 1 April 2017) apply to disputes and offences under Part 3"
         "s 12AA(1A): an employee adopting an April 2025 Scheme child must give the prescribed notice before s 12AA(1)(a) leave"
         "ss 9A(5A)(b), 12A(3)(b)-(4), 12DC(4)(b): the Government-paid benefits are reduced by regulations where the employer is paid back, a father takes elected leave, or the contract ends unused"
         "s 12AD(3)-(4): discretionary reimbursement for an adoptive mother who lacks 3 months' service, eligibility date from 1 November 2021"
